## tools/scripts/setup-student-environment.sh
```bash
#!/bin/bash

# IBM Training Program - Student Environment Setup Script
# This script sets up the development environment for new students

echo "Setting up IBM Training Program environment..."

# Create student directory structure
STUDENT_ID=$1
STUDENT_NAME=$2

if [ -z "$STUDENT_ID" ] || [ -z "$STUDENT_NAME" ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <student-id> <student-name>"
    exit 1
fi

STUDENT_DIR="students/cohort-2025/student-$STUDENT_ID-$STUDENT_NAME"

# Create directory structure
mkdir -p "$STUDENT_DIR"/{certifications/{badges,certificates},projects,documentation,portfolio/{deployed-solutions,code-samples,presentation-materials}}

# Copy templates
cp templates/student-readme-template.md "$STUDENT_DIR/README.md"
cp templates/project-readme-template.md "$STUDENT_DIR/projects/"

# Create weekly project directories
for week in {01..08}; do
    mkdir -p "$STUDENT_DIR/projects/week-$week"
    cp templates/project-readme-template.md "$STUDENT_DIR/projects/week-$week/README.md"
done

# Initialize git tracking
cd "$STUDENT_DIR"
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial student setup for $STUDENT_NAME"

echo "Student environment setup complete for $STUDENT_NAME (ID: $STUDENT_ID)"
echo "Directory created: $STUDENT_DIR"
```

## CONTRIBUTING.md
```markdown
# Contributing to IBM Training Program Repository

## How to Contribute

### For Students
1. Work only in your designated student folder
2. Follow the project submission guidelines
3. Create feature branches for each project
4. Submit pull requests for mentor review
5. Participate in peer code reviews

### For Mentors
1. Review student submissions promptly
2. Provide constructive feedback
3. Update curriculum materials as needed
4. Maintain assessment criteria consistency

### For Program Administrators
1. Manage repository structure
2. Update program documentation
3. Coordinate with IBM partners
4. Track overall program progress

## Code Review Process
1. All submissions require mentor approval
2. Peer reviews are encouraged
3. Feedback should be constructive and specific
4. Code quality standards must be maintained

## Documentation Standards
- All projects must include README files
- Code should be well-commented
- Architecture diagrams required for complex solutions
- User guides for deployed applications
```

